#### Why not use `ObjectStorage`:

It does not support appending, but logs need to be pushed continuously when the task is not finished.

And when the task is finished and there are no more logs, all the logs will be transferred to `ObjectStorage` to avoid wasting database space.

#### Why not use the filesystem directly:

For cluster deployment, we need to avoid using the local filesystem directly. I believe that's also why `ObjectStorage` was designed.

Of course, the local filesystem can be shared by nodes of a cluster, with the help of NFS or something like that.

But @lunny thinks it's not the right way to set a Gitea cluster, there're lots of locking and performance issues.

#### Why not use a table like:

| TaskID | Logs |
| - | - |
| 10 | "aaa\nbbb\nccc\n"|

We also can't append contents to a field on the table.

#### Why not use a table like:

| TaskID | LogIndex | LogLine |
| - | - | - |
| 10 | 0 | "aaa"|
| 10 | 1 | "bbb"|
| 10 | 2 | "ccc"|

I tried, it looked simple but had a lot of annoying problems. See https://github.com/wolfogre/gitea/commit/d7b99e00287ef9756dda3770efcd6bf1cf36485d#diff-f75a1c7ee09e6fc9d0d8e2ebbeb5fc7a188e8fa538abc6dc11982a221679e297

